# PHASE 13: HEALTH AND PRODUCT INFORMATION SAFEGUARDS

Because the platform deals with nutrition and wellness-related products, product accuracy is mandatory.

Do not:

- Claim products cure diseases without authorization.
- Promise treatment results.
- Present supplements as medicines.
- Recommend replacing prescribed medicine.
- Invent ingredients.
- Invent clinical evidence.
- Invent regulatory approvals.
- Invent manufacturer claims.

Store product classification.

Distinguish:
- Nutritional supplements.
- Food products.
- Wellness products.
- Registered medicines, if any.

Only display medicinal claims and registration information when properly verified.

Include appropriate notices that product information does not replace professional medical advice.

Do not collect medical histories or sensitive health information through ordinary product request forms.

